  "hook": "A camera rode a shuttle booster to nearly 3,000 mph and back.",
  "narration": [
    "This camera rode a space shuttle booster to nearly three thousand miles an hour.",
    "It was mounted on one of the two solid rocket boosters, aimed up at the shuttle.",
    "Liftoff. In under two minutes, the readout passed two thousand miles an hour.",
    "Then the boosters burned out and broke away.",
    "Small separation motors fire to push each spent booster clear of the shuttle, so the two never collide.",
    "It kept coasting up to about forty-one miles, with the Earth curving below.",
    "[short pause] Then it fell back, tumbling, at more than two thousand miles an hour.",
    "Then three parachutes opened."
  ],
  "outcome": "And the booster splashed down in the ocean, about four hundred seconds after liftoff.",
